course: dictionary
lesson: 4562
title: Heckle: shouting at a performer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A heckle is a rude or annoying shout made at someone who is speaking or performing in front of a crowd. The clue is in the context: «heckle means shouting comments at a performer». A heckle is aimed at someone on a stage, not at a friend in the playground.
explain: Look at what happens around the word. A heckler shouts to interrupt, so the speaker may stop, and the crowd may laugh or boo. To check your meaning, swap it into a sentence: «The crowd began to heckle the comedian» makes sense if heckle means to shout at him to interrupt.
explain: Heckle can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, you heckle someone. As a noun, a heckle is one of those shouted comments. A person who heckles is called a heckler.
fact: To heckle means to shout rude or annoying comments at someone who is speaking or performing in public.
fact: A heckle is one of those shouted comments.
fact: A heckler is a person who heckles.
fact: Heckling is usually seen as rude, and you may hear it at comedy shows, football matches and political speeches.
fact: A good performer may answer a heckle with a joke.
exercise: The comedian paused when someone at the back began to heckle him. What does heckle mean here? | To clap loudly and cheer | To sing a quiet song | *To shout rude or annoying comments to interrupt | To fall asleep
exercise: Which is true about a heckle? | A ticket to the show | A kind present for the performer | A loud drum | *A shouted comment made to interrupt
exercise: Find and copy one word that means a person who heckles. | crowd | stage | performer | *heckler
test: Why is heckling usually seen as rude? | *It is loud and interrupts someone who is speaking | It makes people laugh at a joke | It helps the speaker remember their words | It is a kind way to clap
test: In the sentence «The crowd gave the singer a heckle», what kind of word is heckle? | A full stop | A verb | An adjective | *A noun
exam: What may a good performer do when a heckler interrupts? | Whisper very softly | Stop the show and go home | *Reply with a joke | Ask the crowd to leave
